`variance::sse` IS C's `madd_epi16` KERNEL **AND** C's ROW PACKING ON x86 NOW
— THE KERNEL FAMILY'S SELF Ir FALLS **52,495,464 -> 19,234,004 (-63.4 %) AT p6
AND 2,436,872,092 -> 1,124,658,211 (-53.9 %) AT p2**, i.e. **5.02x C's
INSTRUCTIONS -> 1.84x** and **2.81x -> 1.30x**, AND THE WHOLE photo_cid FRAME
FALLS **-1.916 % AT p6 AND -1.919 % AT p2** (1,511,826,501 -> 1,482,868,791 and
45,560,540,750 -> 44,686,279,137; port/C 2.143 -> 2.102 and 1.672 -> 1.640),
EVERY RUN BYTE-IDENTICAL — AND THE p6 WALL CLOCK IS **1.010x AGAINST ITS OWN
SAME-BINARY CONTROL** ON A QUIET BOX, WHILE **p2 IS A WALL-CLOCK NULL DESPITE
THE SAME -1.9 % OF INSTRUCTIONS** (§4b). AND ON aarch64 **BOTH** halves LOSE — the generic
body by 1.45x-2.20x and the memory-staged row packing by 1.32x-1.57x — so the
aarch64 arms here are source-identical to `main`'s and BOTH attempts are
recorded as reverted.

AND THE PREMISE THE CHUNK WAS DISPATCHED ON IS REFUTED: **archmage PR #95
REMOVES ZERO BOUNDS CHECKS FROM THIS PORT.** The GOT-resolved
`panic_bounds_check` census is **2,046 sites in all three builds** —
archmage 0.9.28, the #95+#96 stack, and the stack plus this kernel — with
`quant::optimize_b::{closure#0}` at exactly 72 and
`coeff_rate::cost_coeffs_txb_inner::{closure#0}` at 15 in every one of them.
The frame Ir agrees: the patch ALONE is 1,511,826,501 -> 1,511,715,815 at p6
(-0.0073 %) and 45,560,540,750 -> 45,561,373,399 at p2 (**+**0.0018 %) — two
opposite signs inside a hundredth of a percent, i.e. a null.

