    96 streams / 96 decode / 0 rejected
  `inter_completion_scan.sh` with `SCAN_GATE=1` **PASS** — 64 OK, 0 REFUSED, 0 CRASH, 0 other
  the six still reference cells at their pinned sizes: gradient 64x64 q40 p6
    **290 B**, q20 p3 **839 B**, q55 p0 **63 B**, 128x128 q55 p8 **171 B**,
    64x64 q30 p13 **580 B**, screenrep 64x64 q35 p4 **693 B** — 6 OK, 0 BAD
  plus, on the exact committed tree: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets`
    clean of errors and of every warning in the changed files (the two
    `type_complexity` ones the new test raised are fixed with local aliases),
    `rustfmt --edition 2024 --check` clean, `cargo test --doc -p zenav1-svt-dsp`
    0 tests / ok.

A HARNESS TRAP THIS CHUNK PAID FOR, now written into `WORKING-ON-THIS.md` §5:
**a `jj workspace` does not carry the C oracle, and the failure mode is a green
-looking gate that reports a LOWER total.** `capture_c_trace` is a wrapper that
always runs `build.sh` first, and `build.sh` needs BOTH `reference/svt-av1`
(the submodule; a fresh workspace has an empty directory there because
`jj restore` cannot recreate a gitlink) and the gitignored prebuilt
`capture_c_trace.nowrap.bin`. Without them every cell fails as
`[C oracle failed]` — `regression_spotcheck` read **39 / 104** with 65 cells
listed under that string, which is NOT a port defect and looks nothing like
one until you read the bracketed reason. Symlinking `reference/svt-av1` at the
primary checkout and copying the prebuilt driver in took it straight back to
**104 / 104** with no code change. Same shape as the corpus-root trap: **when a
gate reports a smaller total than it does elsewhere, that difference IS the
finding.**


=================== 9. MEMORY (CPU was the priority; report it anyway) ===================

Nothing here allocates: the kernel's only new storage is two `[u8; 16]`
staging arrays on the stack. Measured anyway, with `tools/mem_bisect.sh`
round-robin so box drift lands on both binaries equally, 0 refused rows, both
sides producing the same `.obu` (139,761 B inter / 70,893 B still).

x86_64 r7900x, peak HEAP (heaptrack, LIVE malloc'd bytes), one encode each:
    2048 inter  101.78M -> 101.78M   **UNCHANGED**
    2048 still   61.07M ->  61.07M   **UNCHANGED**
x86_64 r7900x, peak RSS (`/usr/bin/time -v`), 13 round-robin rounds each:
    2048 inter  median 104,588 -> 104,440 KiB (min 104,288 -> 103,916,
                max 105,024 -> 104,720) — distributions overlap completely.
                **A NULL** (the candidate's median is 0.14 % LOWER).
    2048 still  median  69,104 ->  68,772 KiB (min 68,680 -> 68,248,
                max 69,324 -> 69,176) — overlapping. **A NULL.**

aarch64: **not measured, and not needed.** The aarch64 arms in this commit are
source-identical to `7ec5b557`'s (§5), so the 2048-inter arm the memory ceiling
is stated against is not touched by a single instruction. Nothing is pushed
anywhere near 1.20x.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: C's kernel shape with line numbers; the x86 frame and per-function
Ir on photo_cid at p6 and p2, byte-identical on every run; that the archmage
patch ALONE is an Ir null and a bounds-check null; the GOT-resolved census and
its per-function rows; that the generic body is 1.45x-2.20x slower than the
hand NEON arm on an M4 Pro over three alternating runs with disjoint intervals.

Also ESTABLISHED, after the box came free: the x86 wall clock at p6, **1.010x
against its own same-binary control** on a verifiably quiet box (§4b).

NOT ESTABLISHED: **any wall-clock gain at p2** — that row is a NULL against its
control despite -1.919 % of the frame's instructions, and no mechanism for the
disagreement is offered. Also not established: any preset but 6
and 2, any qp but 40, any content but photo_cid, 10-bit (`sse` here is the
8-bit entry; the hbd path is untouched), and whether the row-packed widths 8/4
help at p6 as much as they help at p2.
